      "description": "Where the close sits between the low and high of a range: 0 is the bottom, 100 the top.\n\n- **% of 10-day range** — where a stock sits this fortnight. Rolls with every session.\n- **% of 52-week range** — where it sits over the past year. The closest thing to a valuation read here: dear or cheap against its own history, not against its earnings.\n\nThe 52-week band is a stored snapshot refreshed by hand (`DailyAnalysisMain week52`), so a later close can read below 0 or above 100. That is a stale band, not bad data.",
